= Sybil attack — Technical =

Sybil resistance requires some scarce or externally anchored basis for distinguishing identities or limiting influence. Candidate mechanisms include certification, resource tests, stake/deposits, social trust graphs, device credentials, and rate limits. None is assumption-free: security depends on the adversary model and on what resource or authority cannot be cheaply replicated.

== Modeling cautions ==
* Sybil attack ≠ pseudonymity
* multiple accounts ≠ attack unless used to exploit identity multiplicity
* Sybil resistance ≠ proof of one-human-one-identity in every design

